{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Have I been accustomed?</b> It was fitting for you to consider, since this is not her habit — for none of this has ever happened to you on this road except to indicate that you will not succeed. For even without a serpent, there is a sign."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase שֶׁאַף עַל פִּי שֶׁאֵין נַחַשׁ, יֵשׁ סִימָן likely alludes to the Talmudic dictum (b. Horayot 12a) that even without an explicit omen (נחש), a sign (סימן) may be taken. Rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:45.035515042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}